<title>USA: WHX Corp sees Q4, FY96 loss from strike. [CORRECTED 21:48 GMT]</title>
<headline>WHX Corp sees Q4, FY96 loss from strike. [CORRECTED 21:48 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects from Q1 to Q4 in title.)</p>
<p>WHX Corp said Tuesday it will report a loss in the fourth quarter and the full-year 1996 because of the strike by the United Steelworkers of America.</p>
<p>The strike began October 1 and has now continued for more than 98 days, the company said.</p>
<p>As a result, the company said, no steel products are being made or shipped at eight of its plants in Ohio, Pennsylvania and West Viriginia.</p>
<p>The company said there are no negotiations to end the strike at this time.  </p>
<p>WHX said it had positive cash flow for the fourth quarter and more than $400 million in cash and cash equivalents as of December 31.</p>
</text>
